# RenoEstimate: project rules

## Deployment target
Cloudflare Pages via `@cloudflare/next-on-pages` (`npm run pages:build`; plain `npm run build` stays a standard `next build`).
In the Pages project set the build command to `npx @cloudflare/next-on-pages` and the output directory to `.vercel/output/static`.
Add the `nodejs_compat` compatibility flag in the Pages project settings.

## Edge runtime rules
- Every non-static route (route handlers and dynamic pages) must declare `export const runtime = "edge";` at the very top of the file.
- No Node built-ins (`fs`, `path`, `node:crypto`, `Buffer`, `stream`) in `app/`, `lib/`, `components/` or `hooks/`. Use Web APIs: `fetch`, `Response`, `crypto.subtle`, `TextEncoder`, `URL`.
- `lib/costEstimator.ts` and `lib/design.ts` are pure and must stay free of I/O and Node APIs.
- Secrets are read from `process.env` inside request handlers only, never at module scope, and never in client components (`lib/paddleServer.ts` imports `server-only`).

## Code style
- Strict TypeScript (TypeScript 5), no `any`. Modules stay small, typed and self-documenting.
